"Drahcir" <richwalm@gmail.com> writes:

Greetings, and welcome to rgrn.  

> I'm currently burdened but I don't have anything that I can really
> spare. 

If you're burdened, you carry more stuff with you than you 
need, or you wear too heavy armor, or you are a weakling -- 
which, as a valk, is unlikely.  Most of the stuff one 
finds need not be dragged around, but safely locked away.  

> I've heard that you shouldn't become burdened as much as
> possible in one of the guides I've read. 

That's true.  First, monsters speed up relatively, second 
you get hungry much faster.  At least drop enough to get 
unburdened anytime a monster appears.  

> I need to identify my inventory quick. 

Most unidentified items can be put in a stash, since 
they usually will be only used after identification.  

> What's the fastest way to do this? I don't have any
> identify scrolls on me.

It depends on the stuff.  Many wands give a more or 
less subtle hint for their type when you engrave with 
them.  Uncursed rings do similarly when dropped in 
a sink (but almost surely, they're gone then, so this 
is usually not the best idea), some have immediately 
recognizable effects, and many ring effects can be 
seen by being enlightened while wearing the ring.  
[However, remember to put on uncursed/blessed stuff 
only.]  On Eva Myer's spoiler page you'll find links to 
detailed spoilers about these and other id-ing methods.  

