> I've heard of the word 'Elbreath'

Is that El Cid's morning breath?  Seriously, the word's 
Elbereth, and you should remember the exact wording if 
you want to use it.  

> but can't think of a reason why I would need to use it. All it seems to
> do is stop centain monsters for attacking just like pausing the game or
> can you use this to heal yourself for a while or something? 

Most of the monsters 'respect' Elbereth, that is, if they 
would try to attack you in melee while you are standing on 
a square with the word 'Elbereth' written/engraved/burned 
on it, they will 'turn to flee' instead, being scared and 
trying to get away for some turns.  There are some drawbacks:  

- Your char doesn't write it correctly any time you try, not 
  even if you yourself enter it exactly.  

- Just writing with a soft material is not really enduring, 
  and engraving with harder material usually takes much time 
  in which you're practically defenceless.  

- Some monsters don't respect it, and they usually hit hard.  

- It does not stop ranged attacks.  

Usually, this is used to buy some time, prepare a 
run-away, or to let your pet deal with the critters.  
A crush-happy valk usually has no too much use for it 
unless in an emergency situation (and then only as a 
last resort).  

> Can a
> Valkyrie use these to make new scrolls?

Yes, albeit usually you can only write scrolls you already 
have identified.  (There's a slim chance to write non-ided 
scrolls/spellbooks.)  Useful scrolls to write are eg 
identify, enchant armor/weapon.  

